<h3>二、Reason for Status Change</h3>
<p>UAE Federal Authority for Identity and Citizenship (ICA) has flagged Ms. Vasquez's file based on a medical entry in the Gulf Health Council's database. During her September 2026 visit to Dubai, she received treatment at <b>American Hospital Dubai</b> for acute bronchitis. The ICA requires confirmation that this condition:</p>
<ul>
<li>Is not a communicable disease requiring isolation under UAE Public Health Law</li>
<li>Does not require ongoing treatment that would burden the UAE healthcare system</li>
<li>Has been resolved or is managed with appropriate documentation</li>
</ul>

<h3>三、Required Documents</h3>
<ol>
<li><b>Medical fitness certificate</b> — from a licensed physician stating Ms. Vasquez is fit to travel and poses no public health risk</li>
<li><b>Treatment completion letter</b> — from American Hospital Dubai confirming the September visit is resolved</li>
<li><b>Travel medical insurance</b> — proof of valid insurance covering UAE (minimum $100,000 coverage)</li>
<li><b>Medication list</b> — if carrying prescription medications (with doctor's prescription)</li>
</ol>

