<ul>
<li><b>Denied boarding:</b> Ms. Vasquez will not be allowed on flight EK305</li>
<li><b>Visa-on-arrival revoked:</b> Future UAE entry will require pre-arranged visa</li>
<li><b>No refund:</b> Flight ticket non-refundable under fare rules</li>
<li><b>Immigration record:</b> A "denied entry" stamp on passport (affects future visa applications globally)</li>
</ul>

<h3>六、Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
<p><b>Q: Why is this happening now? I've traveled to Dubai many times.</b><br>
A: The ICA periodically reviews medical records for all visitors. Your September hospital visit triggered a routine review. This is not specific to Ms. Vasquez — approximately 2% of visitors undergo medical documentation review each year.</p>

<p><b>Q: Can I submit documents at the airport?</b><br>
A: No. Medical documentation must be reviewed <b>at least 4 hours before departure</b>. Airport staff cannot override ICA medical flags.</p>

<p><b>Q: What if I don't have the hospital letter from Dubai?</b><br>
A: You can request a duplicate from American Hospital Dubai (medicalrecords@ahd.example). Processing takes 24 hours — which may be too late for tomorrow's flight.</p>

